<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Rio Tinto first half copper output up.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Rio Tinto first half copper output up.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Australian mining giant Rio Tinto Plc/Ltd said in its quarterly report released on Wednesday that mined copper output rose in the six months to June 30 to 378,600 tonnes from 364,000 tonnes in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>Rio Tinto said iron ore output rose to 27.48 million tonnes from 26.45 million tonnes in the same half a year earlier.  </p>
<p>Coal production climbed 33 percent to 39.97 million tonnes in the first half of 1997 from 30.16 million tonnes a year earlier, Rio Tinto said.</p>
<p>The company said its gold production rose by 15 percent to to 1.041 million ounces in the first half of 1997 from 908,000 ounces in the previous corresponding period.</p>
<p>First half aluminium output rose 11 percent to 204,400 tonnes from 184,800 tonnes in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>The company said higher aluminium output was due to the start-up of the third production line at Boyne Island smelter in Australia and the upgrade of Tiwai Point smelter in New Zealand.  </p>
